 "summary": "Family of compact text syntaxes for RDF: Turtle writes triples with prefixes, predicate/object lists, blank-node property lists, collections and literal abbreviations; TriG extends Turtle with named graphs (datasets); Notation3 (N3), the ancestor, adds formulae (quoted graphs), variables, paths and rules for logic.",
 "status": "active",
 "defined_by": [
  "consortium-standard",
  "community-specification"
 ],
 "standards": [
  "W3C RDF 1.1 Turtle (2014)",
  "W3C RDF 1.1 TriG (2014)",
  "W3C RDF 1.2 Turtle (Candidate Recommendation)",
  "W3C N3 Community Group report"
 ],
